    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XUBykx898fZmhehLx2pQdE)_\n\n## Merge order\n- Base: `main` (#466 and #447 are already merged).\n- Touches only `sp-vulpea-ui-view` (`.el`, its literate `.org` section and its test file).\n- Independent of every open PR.\n- Branch is named `469-...` as a guess at the next PR number; if GitHub gave another number, a cloud session cannot rename it.\n\n## Problem\n- In the `vulpea-ui-view` frame the view window is dedicated, so `C-x b` stops with `Cannot switch buffers in a dedicated window` (Emacs `switch-to-buffer`, `switch-to-buffer-in-dedicated-window` is nil).\n- Message taken from Emacs source; not reproduced in a GUI.\n\n## Reading implemented\n- Sia wants to switch buffers from that frame (e.g. jump to another note) and have it work sensibly.\n- New option `sp-vulpea-ui-view-switch-buffer-action`:\n  - `other-window` (default): the chosen buffer opens in the notes window (`sp-vulpea-ui-view--editing-window`) and that frame gets the input focus. The view window stays dedicated and keeps following the current note.\n  - `prompt`: Emacs asks whether to undedicate the view window, then switches in place (the view disappears from that window).\n  - nil: Emacs's own error.\n- An `:around` advice on `switch-to-buffer` acts only when the selected window is the dedicated view window; every other window is untouched. consult, tabspaces and `sp-tabs-switch-to-buffer` all end in `switch-to-buffer`, so they are covered, with the shared buffer list from #466.\n- If the switch fails or is quit, the view window is selected again.\n- With no notes window available, the original runs (so the Emacs error).\n\n## Not tested\n- No Emacs and no GUI in the container: nothing was run. Parentheses balance was checked by script; `.org` blocks match the `.el`.\n- Three new ERT tests (`other-window`, nil error, ordinary window unchanged) were written but not run.\n- Not tried: `consult-buffer` with preview from the view frame, the `prompt` mode, AeroSpace focus change.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [ ] `emacs -Q --batch -l tests/sp-vulpea-ui-view-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes.\n- [ ] Open a note, `M-o v`; in the view frame `C-x b` and pick another buffer: it opens in the main frame, which gets focus; the view stays.\n- [ ] Pick another note this way: the view follows it.\n- [ ] `C-g` at the `C-x b` prompt: nothing changes, view frame stays selected.\n- [ ] `(setopt sp-vulpea-ui-view-switch-buffer-action 'prompt)`: `C-x b` asks to undedicate.\n- [ ] `(setopt sp-vulpea-ui-view-switch-buffer-action nil)`: the \"dedicated window\" error is back.\n- [ ] `C-x b` in an ordinary window behaves as before.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBBnnGabev8xUTfDn1)_",
